Scope note: this license covers every file in this directory.

Compiled with MS C 5.1 (Microsoft Windows 98):
- BMPWIN.bin
- DUALBTN.bin
- EMPTYWIN.bin
- HDRFLGS1.bin
- HDRFLGS2.bin
- HDRFLGS3.bin
- HDRFLGS4.bin
- HDRFLGS5.bin 

Compiled with MS C 5.1 (Microsoft OS/2 1.3):
- CMD_ARGS.bin
- MSG_OS2B.bin

Cross-Compiled with OpenWatcom 2.0 under Linux:
- MSG_OS2A.bin
- MSG_W31.bin

Microsoft shipped no license text
that purports to cover user code compiled with MS C 5.1, and the statically
linked MS C-runtime object code is treated under the same long-standing
practice as the Watcom runtime code below.

The OpenWatcom `.bin` files are compiled with OpenWatcom 2.0 under the
Sybase Open Watcom Public License 1.0; that license plainly governs
OpenWatcom's own source/object code and does not, by its terms, extend to
code you compile with the tool. The status of the small amount of
Watcom-authored C runtime object code (`clibc.lib` etc.) statically linked
into the binaries is a gray area (SOWPL has no explicit runtime-linking
exception), and long-standing practice treats compiled output as unencumbered.
This note documents that caveat; it has not been independently verified
against legal precedent.

The fixture C sources in `testdata/sources/` are unambiguously MIT-covered.
